    "evidence_text": "The extended SAN contains two components: a span detector and a binary classifier for judging whether the question is unanswerable, and both components are jointly optimized.\n\nUsing a multi-task learning approach (c.f.  ), we extend the Stochastic Answer Network (SAN)  for MRC answer span detector to include a classifier that whether the question is unanswerable.\n\nThe two models share the same lower layer to save the number of parameters, and separate the top layers for different tasks (the span detector and binary classifier).\n\nanswer module for the span detector and a one-layer feed forward neural network for the binary classification task.\n\nSpan detector.\n\nWe adopt a multi-turn answer module for the span detector  .\n\nparts: DISPLAYFORM0  Following  , the span loss function is defined: DISPLAYFORM0  The objective function of the binary classifier is defined: DISPLAYFORM0  where INLINEFORM0 is a binary variable: INLINEFORM1 indicates the question is unanswerable and INLINEFORM2 denotes the question is answerable.\n\nImplementation details\tWe utilize spaCy tool to tokenize the both passages and questions, and generate lemma, part-of-speech and named entity tags.\n\nIt shows that it is important to make balance between these two components: the span detector and unanswerable classifier.",
